c neuropathy</article-title><source>Neurology</source><year>1998</year><volume>50</volume><fpage>1842</fpage><lpage>1846</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9633738</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B8"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Sindrup</surname><given-names>SH</given-names></name><name><surname>Andersen</surname><given-names>G</given-names></name><name><surname>Madsen</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name><name><surname>Smith</surname><given-names>T</given-names></name><name><surname>Brosen</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name><name><surname>Jensen</surname><given-names>TS</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Tramadol relieves pain and allodynia in polyneuropathy: a randomised, double-blind, controlled trial</article-title><source>Pain</source><year>1999</year><volume>83</volume><fpage>85</fpage><lpage>90</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10506675</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1016/S0304-3959(99)00079-2</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B9"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Wilder-Smith</surname><given-names>CH</given-names></name><name><surname>Hill</surname><given-names>L</given-names></name><name><surname>Spargo</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name><name><surname>Kalla</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Treatment of severe pain from osteoarthritis with slow-release tramadol or dihydrocodeine in combination with NSAID's: a randomised study comparing analgesia, antinociception and gastrointestinal effects</article-title><source>Pain</source><year>2001</year><volume>91</volume><fpage>23</fpage><lpage>31</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11240075</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1016/S0304-3959(00)00414-0</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B10"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Malonne</surname><given-names>H</give